   "total diffs: 0"). All hits are PRE-EXISTING (OBSERVATIONS, not FAILs):
     - `scrollable-region-focusable` on dashboard@390 (chart data tables)
       and transfers@390 (`.mt-3.overflow-x-auto`) — matches the named
       pre-existing item.
     - `target-size` on major-expenses@390 (approve/reject submit buttons,
       untouched file, not in this branch's diff).
   axe found ZERO `color-contrast` VIOLATIONS anywhere; the dark preset-
   button / 390px KPI-region contrast the brief calls out shows only as an
   axe "incomplete" (manual-review) `color-contrast` finding on Plotly SVG
   chart text (bgOverlap — axe can't resolve contrast against SVG chart
   backgrounds; expected/known limitation) plus one `.text-xl` bgGradient
   item, present on both branch and master. Direct getComputedStyle probe
   of the actual preset-range buttons and `[data-kpi-detail]` links (both
   themes, both viewports) computed 6.99:1 (dark) / 9.37:1 (light) —
   passing 4.5:1; I could not reproduce a sub-4.5:1 hit on the current
   static classes (`text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300` on
   `bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-700`), consistent with this being an
   inactive/JS-driven state not present in the static markup I probed.
   Recorded as OBSERVATION per the "not my call to reclassify a
   already-named pre-existing item" rule — not re-litigated as a FAIL or
   a clean bill; still present in the same form as master.
   axe found ZERO other violations on any LT-touched surface (dashboard,
